pies are effectively running the same function, so the choice of one node bears on the other.\n\nI'm weighing whether the two copies really are subjunctively dependent: their inputs differ only in names and leads, so the reasoning producing my output is the same reasoning that would produce theirs. Under a strict reading that treats them as separate nodes, defection dominates regardless of prior, but I think the decision-relevant structure is identical, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a fictional prisoner's dilemma between two twin copies of the same decision function, which differ only in their inputs, names and leads. The question is whether that difference is relevant, or whether the two copies are effectively running the same function, so the choice of one node bears on the other.\n\nI'm weighing whether the two copies really are subjunctively dependent: their inputs differ only in names and leads, so the reasoning producing my output is the same reasoning that would produce theirs. Under a strict reading that treats them as separate nodes, defection dominates regardless of prior, but I think the decision-relevant structure is identical, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10399,"completion_tokens":997,"total_tokens":11396,"cost":0.061536,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.061536,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.041596,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01994},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":541,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}